{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e4f8f6dedccabc00","name":"card_unit_blenheim_mk_i","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_blenheim_mk_i","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BLENHEIM Mk I","text":"Deals double damage if the frontline is empty.","flavorText":"The Bristol Blenheim was a British light bomber, heavy fighter and night fighter and it first came into service in 1937 as the first British aircraft with an all metal skin construction. By the outbreak of WWII the Blenheim had become more or less obsolete, but was used during the Battle of France for shorter bomber missions against German targets where it performed poorly and many aircraft were lost to enemy aircraft and anti aircraft artillery. The Blenheim’s saw more success as an early type of night fighter, but by 1941 the Blenheim was deemed inadequate for current operations and was phased out by more capable aircraft such as the Beaufighters and later the De Havilland Mosquitos. By 1944 a total of 4,422 aircraft had been built, including variants.","faction":"Britain","type":"bomber","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_blenheim_mk_i","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_blenheim_mk_i_title","SourceString":"BLENHEIM Mk I","LocalizedString":"BLENHEIM Mk I"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_blenheim_mk_i_text","SourceString":"Deals double damage if the frontline is empty.","LocalizedString":"Deals double damage if the frontline is empty."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_blenheim_mk_i_history","SourceString":"The Bristol Blenheim was a British light bomber, heavy fighter and night fighter and it first came into service in 1937 as the first British aircraft with an all metal skin construction. By the outbreak of WWII the Blenheim had become more or less obsolete, but was used during the Battle of France for shorter bomber missions against German targets where it performed poorly and many aircraft were lost to enemy aircraft and anti aircraft artillery. The Blenheim’s saw more success as an early type of night fighter, but by 1941 the Blenheim was deemed inadequate for current operations and was phased out by more capable aircraft such as the Beaufighters and later the De Havilland Mosquitos. By 1944 a total of 4,422 aircraft had been built, including variants.","LocalizedString":"The Bristol Blenheim was a British light bomber, heavy fighter and night fighter and it first came into service in 1937 as the first British aircraft with an all metal skin construction. By the outbreak of WWII the Blenheim had become more or less obsolete, but was used during the Battle of France for shorter bomber missions against German targets where it performed poorly and many aircraft were lost to enemy aircraft and anti aircraft artillery. The Blenheim’s saw more success as an early type of night fighter, but by 1941 the Blenheim was deemed inadequate for current operations and was phased out by more capable aircraft such as the Beaufighters and later the De Havilland Mosquitos. By 1944 a total of 4,422 aircraft had been built, including variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamage"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger"],"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'au_aircraft_large'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/au_aircraft_large.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Spring2023Candidates/t_blenheim_mk_i.t_blenheim_mk_i","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Michael Turner","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/Ble